cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "GCRL-Landscapes"
abstract: >-
  GCRL-Landscapes is a framework for exploring how the hyperparameter
  landscape of offline goal-conditioned reinforcement learning agents evolves
  during training. It samples hyperparameter configurations, trains them in
  consecutive phases, evaluates every run, and provides GP-based landscape
  fitting, cross-goal advantage computation and the complete reproduction
  pipeline for the associated paper's tables.
